cial Education Human Resource Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Woodlands Ribbon Cutting & Public Open House Homecoming Spirit Week Geeks vs. Guardians 5K Fun Run Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Learning Support Instructor (English and Math) Learning Support Instructor (English and Math) DESCRIPTION: Thomas University, an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education with undergraduate and graduate programs in Thomasville, Georgia, seeks applicants for Learning Support Instructors in English and Math. Positions are available on an as needed basis for on-campus instruction. TYPICAL QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree, with earned credits in the subject required. Practical employment experience is preferred. Previous teaching experience preferred but not required. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with  College policy. Ability to work cooperatively with all constituents. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Assist in the development and delivery of subject area content for students. Be available to work 1 to 4 hours per week in the late afternoons, early evenings and/or on Friday mornings. Must complete required elements of the New Faculty Orientation. SUPPLEMENTAL INFORMATION: Math and English instructors work in Learning Support and provide one-on-one and study group support to students, helping them develop subject area knowledge. Instructors support students’ academic achievement by reviewing and clarifying classroom instruction and work closely with the Director of Learning Support and/or subject matter experts to develop and deliver subject area workshops in a variety of delivery modes.  To apply for opportunities, please complete the Thomas University application at www.thomasu.edu/employment . Resumes and cover letters should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this position, please contact Robin DePaola at rouzts@thomasu.edu. TO APPLY: https://apply.appone.com/job/6855a8c561162f6dffdaff7f Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
