U Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Adjunct Faculty in  Humanities, Art, and Music Adjunct Faculty in  Humanities, Art, and Music DESCRIPTION: Thomas University an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education with undergraduate and graduate programs in Thomasville, Georgia seeks applicants for adjunct faculty positions in Humanities, Art, and Music. Positions are available on an as-needed basis for both on-campus and online instruction. TYPICAL QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must hold a master’s degree or Ph.D. in the teaching discipline (or a related field). Practical employment experience is preferred. Previous teaching experience preferred but not required. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with College policy Ability to work cooperatively with all constituents Excellent written and oral communication skills Knowledge of course content SUPPLEMENTAL INFORMATION: To apply for opportunities, please complete the Thomas University application at https://apply.appone.com/job/6a05f99ef061cf2f2d308b07 ;send an email with the subject noting “Humanities, Art, and Music” including curriculum vita, three current references, and official transcripts to Anna Benefield, Office of Human Resources: abenefield@thomasu.edu .  All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this faculty opening, please contact Dr. Jason Dunn at jdunn@thomasu.edu.  For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact Anna Benefield, at abenefield@thomasu.edu . Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida.  Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
